-- Passage rg3-authors-purpose-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a713643f-eef3-5c0a-b28b-094c20190968', 'rg3-authors-purpose-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Clock on Main Street$q$, $q$Long ago, the town of Willow Bend had no clocks on its streets. Most families did not own a watch. People guessed the time by looking at the sun. Because of this, many people were late for the train.

In 1890, a teacher named Ms. Okafor had an idea. She asked the town to build a tall clock on Main Street. Then everyone could see the time. The town liked the idea, but a clock cost a lot of money.

So the people of Willow Bend worked together. Children sold lemonade. Farmers sold extra eggs. Families baked pies for a town fair. After two years, they had saved enough money.

The clock was finished in 1892. It had four faces, so people could read it from every side. A bell rang at the start of each hour. Soon, fewer people missed the train.

The clock still stands on Main Street today. In my opinion, it is the most important thing in Willow Bend. It reminds us what a town can do when people help each other.$q$, 'draft')
